steps.body:
A binary tree is made of nodes. Each node holds a value and points to at most two children, `left` and `right`. A missing child is `null`. Define the node class after `Main`:

```java
class TreeNode {
    int val;
    TreeNode left;
    TreeNode right;
    TreeNode(int val) {
        this.val = val;
    }
}
```

You can link nodes by hand: `TreeNode root = new TreeNode(1);` then `root.left = new TreeNode(2);`. For input, this lesson gives you a finished `readTree` helper. It reads level-order values (top row first, left to right) where `-1` marks a missing child. So `1 2 3 -1 4` is 1 with children 2 and 3, and 2 has only a right child 4.

A depth-first traversal visits every node with recursion. The three orders differ only in when you record the node:

- Preorder: node, left, right.
- Inorder: left, node, right.
- Postorder: left, right, node.

```java
static void preorder(TreeNode node, List<Integer> out) {
    if (node == null) {
        return;
    }
    out.add(node.val);
    preorder(node.left, out);
    preorder(node.right, out);
}
```

Pass one `List<Integer>` down every call so all of them add to the same list.

example.code:
import java.util.ArrayDeque;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Queue;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        TreeNode root = readTree(new Scanner(System.in));
        List<Integer> pre = new ArrayList<>();
        preorder(root, pre);
        List<Integer> in = new ArrayList<>();
        inorder(root, in);
        List<Integer> post = new ArrayList<>();
        postorder(root, post);
        System.out.println("Preorder: " + pre);
        System.out.println("Inorder: " + in);
        System.out.println("Postorder: " + post);
    }

    // Finished helper: reads level-order values (-1 means no child) and builds the tree.
    static TreeNode readTree(Scanner sc) {
        TreeNode dummy = new TreeNode(0); // the first value becomes dummy.right
        Queue<TreeNode> parents = new ArrayDeque<>();
        parents.offer(dummy);
        for (int i = 0; sc.hasNextInt() && !parents.isEmpty(); i++) {
            int value = sc.nextInt();
            TreeNode node = value == -1 ? null : new TreeNode(value);
            if (i % 2 == 1) {
                parents.peek().left = node;
            } else {
                parents.poll().right = node;
            }
            if (node != null) {
                parents.offer(node);
            }
        }
        return dummy.right;
    }

    static void preorder(TreeNode node, List<Integer> out) {
        if (node == null) {
            return;
        }
        out.add(node.val);
        preorder(node.left, out);
        preorder(node.right, out);
    }

    static void inorder(TreeNode node, List<Integer> out) {
        if (node == null) {
            return;
        }
        inorder(node.left, out);
        out.add(node.val);
        inorder(node.right, out);
    }

    static void postorder(TreeNode node, List<Integer> out) {
        if (node == null) {
            return;
        }
        postorder(node.left, out);
        postorder(node.right, out);
        out.add(node.val);
    }
}

class TreeNode {
    int val;
    TreeNode left;
    TreeNode right;
    TreeNode(int val) {
        this.val = val;
    }
}

